IO-14: reject culvert codes outside 0 - 57

handle_xsections() stored any positive culvert code and silently ignored
negative ones. A code above 57 skips the normal-flow limitation in
DynamicWave.cpp (culvert branch for code > 0) while Culvert.cpp ignores it,
as in legacy. Report ERR_NUMBER for codes outside 0 - 57, as the 5.3.0 patch
does (legacy already rejected negative codes).

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-14_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp b/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
index c205c9e..4e7fbad 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/handlers/LinksHandler.cpp
@@ -501,7 +501,9 @@ void handle_xsections(SimulationContext& ctx, const std::vector<std::string>& li
         // Culvert code (optional, token 7)
         if (tok.size() > 7 && cr >= 0) {
             int cc = static_cast<int>(to_double(tok[7]));
-            if (cc > 0)
+            if (cc < 0 || cc > 57)   // culvert codes are 1 - 57 (legacy link.c)
+                ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(ERR_NUMBER, tok[7]));
+            else if (cc > 0)
                 ctx.link_subtypes.conduits.culvert_code[static_cast<std::size_t>(cr)] = cc;
         }
     }
